# Geometry optimization of LiH as its own workflow: `--wf=optimize`.
#
# This is the composable form of a geometry optimization -- one task that drives
# MolOpt over a reference engine and publishes the optimized geometry into the
# StepContext, as opposed to `dft gopt 1`, which optimizes inside a single SCF
# task (see scf_lih_gopt for that form; the two produce the same geometry).
#
# The reference engine is chosen by `optimization method` -- moldft here, nemo in
# optimize_lih_nemo. Everything else in this deck is identical between the two,
# which is the point: both engines are driven by the same optimizer through the
# same code path.
#
# The `optimization` group is what governs the optimizer. Any threshold left unset
# is derived from the wavefunction accuracy (protocol().back(), Dalton-style), so
# the 1e-6 rung is what puts gtol at 1e-5; a deck that sets `gtol` explicitly wins
# over that. See `madqc --print_parameters=optimization`.
#
# Starts 0.015 bohr inside the HF minimum, which the optimizer closes in two steps.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc --wf=optimize optimize_lih_moldft.in)

optimization
    method      moldft
    maxiter     10
end

dft
    xc          hf
    protocol    [1e-4, 1e-6]
    dconv       1e-4
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    eprec   1e-6
    Li  0.0  0.0  0.0
    H   0.0  0.0  3.05
end
